1 NOTE Ruy Gomes de Silva fought in the conquest of Tangiers in 1437 and in 1445 he was within the Portugese column that helped John II of Castile against the Infantes of Aragon. In 1449 he was given, via Cedula Real, the village of Ulme
2 CONC  near Santarem. This Cedula was one of Perpetuity. Ruy died 1487. He was married to Blanca de Almeida. Juan de Silva inherited all of his father's holdings.
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT GF Cokayne with Vicary Gibbs H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, Editors, The Complete Peereage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Bitain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct or Dormant
