2 CONT *8.          SANCHO Manuel ([1283]-before 1346).  Señor de Infantado y Carrión.  Adelantado Mayor of Murcia.  Beneficiary under his father’s 20 Dec 1283 will.  The Chronicon Domini Joannis Emmanuelis records that “Sancius Emmanuel
2 CONC , germanus suus, ac Ægidius Roderici de Miño, necnon Fr. Joannes G. de Arevalo” confirmed the foundation by “Dns Joannes” of “Ecclesiam Prædictorum Rupis-fidelis” in 1324[1354].  <br> ''m'' INÉS García de Toledo, daughter of DIEGO
2 CONC  García, Almirante of Castile & his wife María García Señora de Magán y Mejorada.  Living a widow in 1346.  Sancho & his wife had four children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT **a)         JUAN Sánchez Manuel (after 1325-Alcaraz 1390).  Conde de Carrión 1368. <br> ''m'' (after 1350) JUANA de Ejérica, daughter of PEDRO de Ejérica [Aragón] Baron de Ejérica & his wife Bonaventura di Arborea.  Juan & his wi
2 CONC fe had three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT ***i)          ALFONSO (-after 1393).  Conde de Carrión.
2 CONT
2 CONT ***ii)          LEONOR.  She succeeded her brother as Condesa de Carrión.  ''m'' JUAN Fernández de Padilla.
2 CONT
2 CONT ***iii)         INÉS.  ''m'' GARCI Fernández de Villodre.
2 CONT
2 CONT **b)         BEATRIZ Sánchez Manuel.  ''m'' PEDRO de Lando. 
2 CONT
2 CONT **c)          INÉS Fernández de Villena.  ''m'' ÍÑIGO López de Mendoza Señor de Castilnovo, son of ---.
2 CONT
2 CONT **d)         FERNANDO Sánchez Manuel (-1407).  Bishop of Calahorra.  Abbot at Valladolid.  If the following marriage is correct, Fernando presumably resigned his ecclesiastical appointments. <br> ''m'' CATERINA Sánchez Señora de P
2 CONC inilla. 
