1 NOTE Ruy Gomez de Silva, hijodalgo de la casa infante de Portugal 1457 (Santaren)
2 CONT Prince of Eboli. Worked in the royal house of Phillip. Ruy Gomez de Silva entered the order of la Calatrava in 1540. He had to relinquish his membership within the order of La Alcantra.
2 CONT During 1558 Ruy received properties in the Canary Islands, in Tenerife and Villena.
2 CONT In July 1559 Ruy was granted the title, Prince of Eboli. 30 April 1571 named as Clavero of the Order of the Calatrava by Philip II
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT Luis de Salazar y Castro: Historia genealogica de casa de Silva, Madrid 1685, Vol II pg 442 - 450.
2 CONT Archivo Historico Nacional, Madrid, seccion Osuna, Legato 2024, no. 13(1), 13(2) -13(4)
2 CONT Luis Cabrera de Cordoba: Historia de Felipe II, Rey de Espagna, Madrid 1876 - 1877, Vol II, book 10, pg 141-142.
2 CONT James M. Boydon: The Courier and the King, Ruy Gomez de Silva, Philip II and the court of Spain. Univ of California Press, Berkley, Los Angeles-Oxford c1995 1995.
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT Manuel Joao da Costa Felgueiras Gaio, "Nobiliario das Famílias de Portugal", Tomo Vigésimo Primeiro, Título de Monizes, § 17, § 18 e § 19
2 CONT Various Authors, "Armorial Lusitano", p. 370-2, Lisbon, 1961
2 CONT Dom Augusto Romano Sanches de Baena e Farinha de Almeida Portugal Sousa e Silva, 1.º Visconde de Sanches de Baena, "Archivo Heraldico-Genealógico", Volume II, p. CXV, Lisbon, 1872
2 CONT Cristóvão Alão de Morais, "Pedatura Lusitana", Volume I (reformulated edition), p. 668-70
2 CONT Archivo General de Simancas.SIG: Patronato Real, Caja 49, Doc 82.
2 CONT ES.47161.AGS/3.2.6/
2 CONT Instruccion de Reina Catolica a Gui Gomez, para tratar sobre la paz con la infanta Beatriz de Portugal.
2 CONT 1480
