1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sancho of Alburquerque (1342 - 1375) is known in Spanish as Sancho de Castilla, Infante de Castilla, 1. Conde de Alburquerque.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the ninth of the ten illegitimate children of King Alfonso XI of Castile and Lady Eleanor of Guzman.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in Seville. He participated in a revolt of the Castilian nobles against the despotic rule of his brother Pedro of Castile.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1373 he married Beatrice of Portugal, daughter of Peter I of Portugal and Ines de Castro. They had two children: Fernando Sanchez, 2nd Count of Alburquerque, and Eleanor of Alburquerque, who married Ferdinand I of Aragon.
2 CONT
2 CONT He also had an illegitimate daughter, Eleanor Sanchez of Castile
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sancho_of_Alburquerque
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancho Enríquez de Castilla of Alburquerque (1342 - 1375) is known in Spanish as Don Sancho Enríquez de Castilla, Infante de Castilla, 1. Conde de Alburquerque.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the ninth of the ten illegitimate children of King Alfonso XI of Castile and Lady Eleanor of Guzman.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in Seville. He participated in a revolt of the Castilian nobles against the despotic rule of his brother Pedro of Castile.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1373 he married Beatrice of Portugal, daughter of Peter I of Portugal and Inês de Castro. They had two children: Don Fernando Sánchez, 2nd Count of Alburquerque, and Doña Eleanor of Alburquerque, who married Ferdinand I of Arag
2 CONC on.
2 CONT
2 CONT He also had an illegitimate daughter, Doña Leonor Sánchez de Castilla.
2 CONT
2 CONT This article draws heavily on the September 2005 version of the corresponding article in the Spanish-language Wikipedia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Retrieved from "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sancho,_1st_Count_of_Alburquerque"
2 CONT
2 CONT Categories: 1342 births | 1375 deaths | People from Seville | 14th-century Spanish people | Spanish nobility
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancho of Alburquerque
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancho of Alburquerque (1342 - 1375) is known in Spanish as Sancho de Castilla, Infante de Castilla, 1. Conde de Alburquerque.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the ninth of the ten illegitimate children of King Alfonso XI of Castile and Lady Eleanor of Guzman.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in Seville. He participated in a revolt of the Castillian nobles against the despotic rule of his brother Pedro of Castile.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1373 he married Beatrice of Portugal, daughter of Peter I of Portugal and Ines de Castro. They had two children: Fernando Sanchez, 2nd Count of Alburquerque, and Eleanor of Alburquerque, who married Ferdinand I of Aragon.
2 CONT
2 CONT He also had an illegitimate daughter, Eleanor Sanchez of Castile.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT De Wikipedia:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancho de Castilla, el noveno de los diez hijos extramatrimoniales de Alfonso XI y su amante Leonor de Guzmán, nació en la ciudad de Sevilla en 1342. Su padre falleció en 1350 y le sucedió en el trono su hijo legítimo, Pedro I.
2 CONT
2 CONT En abril de 1366, su hermano Enrique, que se hallaba en guerra con Pedro I, le nombró conde de Alburquerque, señor de Ledesma, de Alba de Liste, de Medellín, Tiedra y Montalbán. Junto con sus hermanos Enrique (futuro Enrique II de
2 CONC  Castilla), Fadrique y Tello, Sancho luchó contra su hermanastro Pedro I.
2 CONT
2 CONT También participó en la sublevación de los nobles castellanos, motivados por el descontento que produjeron los crímenes del rey Pedro, quien pasaría a la historia con el sobrenombre de «el Cruel».
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sancho Alfonso de Castilla (1342–1374) is known in Spanish as Don Sancho Alfonso de Castilla, Infante de Castilla, I conde de Alburquerque.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the ninth of the ten illegitimate children of King Alfonso XI of Castile and Lady Eleanor de Guzmán.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in Seville. He participated in a revolt of the Castilian nobles against the despotic rule of his brother, Pedro of Castile.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1373 he married Beatrice of Portugal, daughter of Peter I of Portugal and Inês de Castro. They had two children: Fernando Sánchez, 2nd Count of Alburquerque, and Eleanor of Alburquerque, who married Ferdinand I of Aragon.
2 CONT
2 CONT He also had an illegitimate daughter, Leonor Sánchez de Castilla, who married Fadrique de Castilla y Ponce de Leon, illegitimate son of Henry II, King of Castile. Ancestors
