1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Señora de Torrejón de Velasco
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Heredó el señorío de Torrejón de Velasco. Este matrimonio son los bisabuelos de Garcia Alvarez de Toledo y Carrillo de Toledo, I Duque de Alba.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SPANISH%20NOBILITY%20LATER%20MEDIEVAL%202.htm#LeonorAyalaMFernandoAlvarezToledo
2 CONT
2 CONT *1.         PEDRO López de Ayala .  His ancestry is set out by Argote Molina[4].  Señor de Unza, Mena y Albudeite.  Adelantado mayor of the kingdom of Murcia.  Mistress (1):  INÉS de Azagra, daughter of ---.  Pedro had two illegit
2 CONC imate children by Mistress (1):  …
2 CONT **b)         [5]FERNANDO Pérez (-after 2 Dec 1378[6], bur Quijana, Torre de Ayala).  Señor del Valle de Ayala.  [7].  Ayala´s Crónica de Pedro I records that King Pedro I granted “una tierra...las Encartaciones...cerca de Vizcaya”
2 CONC  to “Don Ferrand Perez de Ayala” in 1351[8].  He was the author of a genealogical treatise on his family 'Libro del linaje de los señores de Ayala'[9], completed by his son.  m ELVIRA Álvarez de Ceballos, daughter of DIEGO Gutiérr
2 CONC ez de Ceballos & his wife Juana García Carrillo[10] (-before 1372, bur Quijana, Torre de Ayala).  Fernando & his wife had five children:  …
2 CONT ***iv)       '''LEONOR''' de Ayala .  Señora de Torrejón de Velasco.  Her marriage is confirmed by the charter dated 11 Sep 1441 which her daughter "Doña Maria de Ayala hija de Fernán Álvarez de Toledo señor de Hijares y de doña T
2 CONC eresa de Ayala señora de Pinto" issued relating to "su heredad de Dosbarruelos, término de Toledo"[13].  m (1366) '''FERNANDO''' Álvarez de Toledo Señor de Valdecorneja, son of --- GARCÍA Álvarez de Toledo & his wife Mencia de Men
2 CONC eses (-near Lisbon 1384).
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SPANISH%20NOBILITY%20LATER%20MEDIEVAL%202.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.         GARCÍA Álvarez de Toledo .  Alcalde mayor de Toledo.  m MENCÍA de Meneses, daughter of ---.  García & his wife had three children:  
2 CONT ** a)         GARCÍA Álvarez de Toledo (-Ciudad Rodrigo 1370).  Señor de Oropesa, Valdecorneja, Piedrahita y Horcajada 8 Jun 1369.  Master of the Order of Santiago 1359, resigned 1366.  
2 CONT ** b)         ---.  m ---.  One child:  
2 CONT *** i)          FERNANDO Álvarez de Toledo .  Señor de Oropesa.  m ELVIRA de Ayala, daughter of --- (-after 17 Aug 1400).  "Diego Hurtado de Mendoza almirante de Castilla" granted "unas casas en Toledo a su prima doña Elvira Ayala
2 CONC , mujer de Fernán Álvarez de Toledo II señor de Oropesa" by charter dated 17 Aug 1400[1].   -         CONDES de OROPESA.  
2 CONT ** c)         '''FERNANDO''' Álvarez de Toledo (-near Lisbon 1384).  Señor de Valdecorneja.  Mariscal de Castilla.  He died of the plague.  m (1366) '''LEONOR''' de Ayala Señora de Torrejón de Velasco, daughter of FERNANDO Pérez d
2 CONC e Ayala & his wife Elvira de Ceballos.  Her marriage is confirmed by the charter dated 11 Sep 1441 which her daughter "Doña Maria de Ayala hija de Fernán Álvarez de Toledo señor de Hijares y de doña Teresa de Ayala señora de Pinto
2 CONC " issued relating to "su heredad de Dosbarruelos, término de Toledo"[2].  Fernando & his wife had two children:  
2 CONT *** i)          GARCÍA Álvarez de Toledo .  Señor de Valdecorneja.  m CONSTANZA Sarmiento, daughter of ---.  -         CONDES de ALBA de TORRES, DUQUES de ALBA.  
2 CONT *** ii)         MARÍA de Ayala (-after 11 Sep 1441).  "Doña Maria de Ayala hija de Fernán Álvarez de Toledo señor de Hijares y de doña Teresa de Ayala señora de Pinto" issued a charter dated 11 Sep 1441 relating to "su heredad de 
2 CONC Dosbarruelos, término de Toledo"[3].  
