1 OCCU Señor de Villena. Príncipe de Villena, Señor de Escalona, Señor de Peñafiel, Mayordomo mayor del rey
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Don Juan Manuel (1282-1348); II señor de Villena, Escalona y de Peñafiel, primer duque y príncipe de Villena. Heredero de las posesiones paternas, fue Mayordomo mayor de Fernando IV el Emplazado y tutor de Alfonso 
2 CONC XI de Castilla durante su minoría de edad. A su muerte fue sepultado en el Convento de San Pablo de Peñafiel que había fundado.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manuel_de_Castilla#Matrimonios_y_descendencia
2 CONT
2 CONT Fue uno de los principales exponentes de la prosa medieval de ficcion, autor de "El Conde Lucanor".  Uno de los hombres más poderosos de su época, acuñó su propia moneda, mantuvo él solo un ejército de 1000 caballeros, Príncipe, S
2 CONC eñor y Duque de Villena.  Entre sus hijos más tardios figura nuestro Enrique Manuel de Villena, quien pasa a vivir en Portugal.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CASTILE.htm#JuanManueldied1348B<br/>
2 CONT Don JUAN Manuel "el Scritor", son of Infante don MANUEL de Castilla y León, Señor de Villena, Escalona and Peñafiel, & his second wife Béatrix de Savoie (Escalona 5 May 1282-Córdoba 13 Jun 1348, bur Peñafiel, monastery of San Pabl
2 CONC o).  The Chronicon Domini Joannis Emmanuelis records the birth in May 1282 of “Dns Joannes, filius Dni Emmanuelis in Escalona”[1343].  He succeeded his father in 1283 as Señor de Villena, Escalona, Elche, Peñafiel, Cartagena, Lorc
2 CONC a, Castillo del Garci-Múñoz, Alcocer, Salmerón, Valdeolivas, Cuéllar y Almenara.  The Chronicon Domini Joannis Emmanuelis records that “Rex Dns Fernandus” gave Alarcón to “Dno. Joanni” in exchange for Elche in Feb 1298[1344].  The
2 CONC  Chronicon Domini Joannis Emmanuelis records that “Rex Fernandus” gave “Aymesta” to “Dno Joanni” in May 1304, and restored his control over Alarcón in Feb 1306[1345].  The Chronicon Domini Joannis Emmanuelis records that “Dns Joan
2 CONC nes” began the siege of “Pennam-fidelem” in Jul 1307[1346].  Mayordomo Mayor of King Fernando IV of Castile.  Mayordomo Mayor of Kings Fernando IV and Alfonso XI of Castile 25 Mar 1311-1 Mar 1314.  "Infanta Donna Blanca fija del…r
2 CONC ey Don Alfonso, Sennora de las Huelgas" sold various properties to "Don Johan fijo del…Infant Don Manuel" by charter dated Aug 1312[1347].  Edward II King of England wrote to “domino Johanni Manuelis filio domini Infantis Manuelis
2 CONC  de Ispania, consanguineo regis Angliæ” requesting his support in certain negotiations by charter dated 1 Apr 1324[1348].  The Chronicon Domini Joannis Emmanuelis records that “Dns Joannes filius Infantis Dni Emmanuelis et Dns Joa
2 CONC nnes filius Infantis Dni Joannis” renounced their tutorship over King Alfonso XI in Aug 1325[1349].  He led several periods of rebellion against King Alfonso XI, notably after the latter's repudiation of his daughter Constanza in 
2 CONC 1327.  Adelantado Mayor on the border with Andalucía, and in the Kingdom of Murcia.  He was an author of note, his works included El Conde Lucanor and El Libro de los Estados[1350].   
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly (contract Perpignan 21 Nov 1299, Requena Jan 1300) Infanta doña ISABEL de Mallorca, daughter of JAIME II King of Mallorca [Aragón] & his wife Esclarmonde de Foix (Montpellier [1280]-Alicante after 10 Oct 1301 or Es
2 CONC calona Dec 1301).  The Crónica de San Juan de la Peña names "la primera…Isabel…la otra Sancha" as the two daughters of Jaime King of Mallorca, stating that Isabel was the wife of "Don Johan Manuel"[1351].  The Chronicon Domini Joa
2 CONC nnis Emmanuelis records the marriage in Jan 1300 of “Dns Joannes” and “Infantissa Dna Elisabeth filia Regis Majoricarum, in Requena”[1352].  The Chronicon Domini Joannis Emmanuelis records the death in Dec 1301 of “Dna Infantissa 
2 CONC in Escalona”[1353]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly (Játiva 2 Apr 1312) Infanta doña CONSTANZA de Aragón, daughter of JAIME II King of Aragon & his second wife Blanche di Sicilia [Anjou] (Valencia 1 Apr 1300-Castillo de Garci-Múñoz 19 Aug 1327).  The Crónica de San
2 CONC  Juan de la Peña names "la primera…Doña Maria…la segunda Doña Costança…la tercera…Doña Isabel…la quarta…Doña Blancha…la quinta…Doña Violante" as the five daughters of King Jaime II and his wife Blanca, stating that Constanza was t
2 CONC he wife "Don Juan fillo del infant Don Manuel"[1354].  The Chronicon Domini Joannis Emmanuelis records the marriage in Apr 1312 of “Dns Joannes cum Infantissa Dna Constantia in Xativa”[1355].  The Chronicon Domini Joannis Emmanuel
2 CONC is records the death in Aug 1327 of “Infantissa Dna Constantia in Castella”[1356].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' thirdly (Lerma Jan 1329) BLANCA de la Cerda Señora de Lara y Vizcaya, daughter of FERNANDO [II] de la Cerda Señor de Palenzuela & his wife Juana Núñez de Lara “la Palomilla” ([1311]-1347).  The Nobiliario of Pedro Conde de
2 CONC  Barcelos names "D. Juan Nuñez, D. Margarita monja, D. Blanca" as the children of "D. Fernando de la Cerda" and his wife "D. Iuana Nuñez la Palomilla, viuda del Infante D. Enrique", another passage recording that "D. Juan Manuel" 
2 CONC married "D. Blanca de la Cerda"[1357].  The Chronicon Domini Joannis Emmanuelis records the marriage in Jan 1329 of “Dns Joannes cum Dna Blanca, filia Dni Fernandi in Lerma”[1358]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mistress''' (1): INÉS González de Castañeda, daughter of RUY Díaz de Castañeda & his wife María Ruiz Ceballos. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mistress''' (2): ---.  The name of the second mistress of Juan Manuel is not known. 
