2 CONT Prince Afonso, Lord of Portalegre
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT   (Redirected from Infante Afonso, Lord of Portalegre)
2 CONT
2 CONT Infante Afonso of Portugal (Portuguese pronunciation: [ɐˈfõsu]; English: Alphonzo or Alphonse) was a Portuguese infante (prince), son of King Afonso III of Portugal and his second wife Beatrice of Castile. He was titled Lord of Po
2 CONC rtalegre, Castelo de Vide, Arronches, Marvão and Lourinhã.
2 CONT
2 CONT Afonso was born on February 8, 1263 and in 1287 married Violante of Castile, daughter of Castilian Infante Juan Manuel of Castile.
2 CONT
2 CONT Afonso died on November 2, 1312 in Lisbon.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Issue
2 CONT
2 CONT By his wife Violante Manuel of Castile he had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Infante Afonso, Lord of Leiria
2 CONT
2 CONT Infanta Maria, Lady of Menezes and Orduña
2 CONT
2 CONT Infanta Isabel, Lady of Penela
2 CONT
2 CONT Infanta Constança of Portalegre
2 CONT
2 CONT Infanta Beatriz, Lady of Lemos
2 CONT
2 CONT   Infante dom AFONSO de Portugal ([Lisbon] 8 Feb 1263-Lisbon 2 Nov 1312, bur Lisbon Dominican monastery).  The Chronicon Conimbricensi records the birth “VIII Id Feb” in 1263 of “Infans Doñs Alfonsus filius Regis Domni Alfonsi et 
2 CONC Reginæ Domnæ Beatricis”[108].  Senhor de Portoalegre Castel-de-Vides Ourem Sintra Marvam e Arronches Leyra and Lourignan 1299.  Governor of Guarda Lamego and Viseu.  m ([1287]) doña VIOLANTE Manuel de Castilla, daughter of Infante
2 CONC  don JUAN Manuel de Castilla Duque de Penafiel y Escalona & his first wife Infanta doña Constanza de Aragón ([1265]-Lisbon 1314, bur Lisbon Dominican monastery).  The mid-14th Century Nobiliario of don Pedro de Portugal Conde de B
2 CONC arcelós names “doña Violante, hija del infante don Manuel de Castilla é de la infanta doña Constanza de Aragon” as wife of “el infante don Alonso de Portugal”[109].  Señora de Elda, Novelda, Medellín y ½ Peñafiel.  Infante dom Afo
2 CONC nso & his wife had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT a)             dom AFONSO de Portugal ([1288]-1300).  Senhor de Leiria.
2 CONT
2 CONT b)             dona MARIA de Portugal ([1290]-).  The mid-14th Century Nobiliario of don Pedro de Portugal Conde de Barcelós records that “don Fernando” married “doña Maria, hija del infante don Alonso de Portugal é de doña Violan
2 CONC te hija del Infante don Manuel”, adding that she had previously married “don Tello”[110].  m firstly ([1308/12]) don TELLO Afonso de Meneses 8th Señor de Meneses, Montealegre y San Ramón, son of don ALFONSO Téllez de Molina [Casti
2 CONC lla] 7th Señor de Meneses & his wife doña Teresa Pérez de Asturias (-Tardejas 1315).  m secondly (1315) don FERNANDO Díaz de Haro, Señor de Orduña y Valmaseda, son of don DIEGO López de Haro Señor Soberano de Vizcaya, Señor de Har
2 CONC o & his wife Infante doña Violante de Castilla. 
2 CONT
2 CONT c)             dona ISABEL de Portugal ([1292]-shortly before 1367).  The mid-14th Century Nobiliario of don Pedro de Portugal Conde de Barcelós records that “don Juan el Tuerto” married “doña Isabel, hija del infante don Alonso d
2 CONC e Portugal é de doña Violante, hija del infante don Manuel de Castilla é de la infanta doña Constanza de Aragon”[111].  Senhora de Pinella e Miranda.  m don JUAN de Castilla "el Tuerto" Señor Soberano de Vizcaya, son of Infante do
2 CONC n JUAN de Castilla y León Señor de Valencia de Campos & his second wife doña María Díaz de Haro Señora Soberana de Vizcaya (after 1293[112]-murdered Toro 2 Dec 1326).   
2 CONT
2 CONT d)             dona COSTANÇA de Portugal ([1294]-).  m ([1295], not consummated) don NUÑO González de Lara, son of don JUAN Núñez de Lara & his second wife doña Teresa Díaz de Haro ([1284]-Valladolid 1296).  Alférez of don Fernand
2 CONC o IV "el Ajurno" King of Castile 3 Aug 1295 to 1296. 
2 CONT
2 CONT e)             dona BRITES de Portugal ([1298]-).  m as his first wife, don PEDRO Fernández de Castro "él de la Guerra" Señor de Lemos y Sarria, son of don Fernán Rodríguez de Castro & doña Violante Sánchez de Castilla (-killed in
2 CONC  battle near Algeciras early Jun 1342).
