2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louren%C3%A7o_de_Almeida
2 CONT
2 CONT Lourenço de Almeida (c.1480 - March 1508[1]) was a Portuguese explorer and military commander.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in Martim, Kingdom of Portugal, the son of Francisco de Almeida, first viceroy of Portuguese India. Acting under his father, Lourenço distinguished himself in the Indian Ocean, and made Ceylon (present Sri Lanka) tribu
2 CONC tary to Portugal (see Portuguese Ceylon). He belonged to the Order of Christ.
2 CONT
2 CONT He made the first Portuguese voyage to Ceylon in 1505 and established a settlement there, thus permitting the expansion of the Portuguese Empire in Asia.
2 CONT
2 CONT He defeated the fleet of the samorin at the Battle of Cannanore in 1506. Two years later however, he died in a naval action off Chaul, in India, at the Battle of Chaul.
